{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.wedderburn_trace_identity","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QBesselContiguityRecurrence"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.realization_discriminating_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.realization_discriminating_block","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L161-L172","doc":"**The discriminating test (machine-checked form of the s013 scope-note kill-test).**\nFor any block whose q-dimension has the self-conjugate `(3,1,1)` shape\n`d_q · [2]_q = [4]_q · [3]_q` (proved for the actual hook data in `shape_311`), a\nrealization forces the radial weight at its lattice point to satisfy\n`w · D · [2]_q = [4]_q · [3]_q`.  A candidate `latticePt` that fits the three\nsingle-q-integer blocks but misses this product at the self-conjugate block is wrong. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.realization_on_orbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.realization_on_orbit","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L147-L159","doc":"**Any realization puts the whole vacuum row on a single q-Bessel coefficient orbit**:\n`S0 p = weight 0 · ∏_{j < latticePt p} r_j` with `r_j` the second-kind contiguity ratio.\nThis is the falsifiable content of the obligation — the `S0` values are not free, they are\none orbit of the corpus's q-Bessel recurrence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.realizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.realizes","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L145-L145","doc":"**The realization**: the radial weight at the partition point is the vacuum row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.latticePt_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.latticePt_conj","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L143-L143","doc":"Transpose-equivariance: `λ` and `λ′` share a lattice point (precheck P2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.weight_qbessel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.weight_qbessel","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L139-L139","doc":"`weight` solves the Jackson second-kind q-Bessel contiguity — the corpus-formalized\nconstraint (`QBesselContiguityRecurrence`) making this carrier content-bearing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.weight","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L136-L136","doc":"The radial weight family (second-kind radial part). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.latticePt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.latticePt","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L134-L134","doc":"Partition → q-Bessel-lattice point (the open DG construction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.QBesselRadialPartRealization","kind":"class","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L115-L145","doc":"**Conjecture carrier (OPEN — the s013 / precheck step-(a) obligation): the q-Bessel\nradial-part realization of the keystone vacuum row.**  A realization supplies:\n\n* `latticePt` — the partition → q-Bessel-lattice assignment.  **This map is the open\n  geometric construction** (the owner-gated DG object, #2503); it is NOT established\n  anywhere in the corpus, and this class does not assert it exists.\n* `weight` — the radial weight family, **constrained** to the corpus-formalized Jackson\n  second-kind q-Bessel contiguity (the hypothesis of\n  `QOU.QBeta.qbessel_second_kind_coeff_closed_form`).  This constraint is the content:\n  a solution family is a single coefficient orbit, so all vacuum-row values must lie on\n  ONE q-Bessel orbit (`realization_on_orbit`) — falsifiable, not an arbitrary table.\n* `latticePt_conj` — transpose-equivariance, the `W_λ = W_{λ′}` hallmark the measure must\n  respect (precheck P2).\n* `realizes` — the weight at each partition's lattice point IS the vacuum row `S0`.\n\nNo instance is provided: the open state is the honest state (§3b-tax).  The discriminating\nnumerical test a candidate must pass is `realization_discriminating_block` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.dq_311_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.dq_311_div","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L106-L111","doc":"The division form of the discriminating block:\n`d_q(3,1,1) = [5]_q!/∏hooks = [4]_q[3]_q/[2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shape_311","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shape_311","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L98-L104","doc":"**`d_q(3,1,1) = [4]_q[3]_q/[2]_q`** (multiplicative form):\n`[5]_q! · [2]_q = [4]_q · [3]_q · ∏ hooks(3,1,1)`.  The electron block — the sole\nself-conjugate class at `n = 5` and the only `d_q` that is NOT a single balanced\nq-integer.  The realization difficulty is concentrated here (value-map screen #3197). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shape_32","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shape_32","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L93-L96","doc":"**`d_q(3,2) = [5]_q`** (multiplicative form): `[5]_q! = [5]_q · ∏ hooks(3,2)`.\nThe muon block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shape_41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shape_41","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L88-L91","doc":"**`d_q(4,1) = [4]_q`** (multiplicative form): `[5]_q! = [4]_q · ∏ hooks(4,1)`.\nThe standard-representation family `d_q(n−1,1) = [n−1]_q` at `n = 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shape_row5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shape_row5","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L84-L86","doc":"**`d_q(5) = [1]_q = 1`** (multiplicative form): `[5]_q! = ∏ hooks(5)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hookProd311","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hookProd311","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L80-L82","doc":"Hook-length product of the self-conjugate `λ = (3,1,1)`: hooks `{5,2,2,1,1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hookProd32","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hookProd32","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L76-L78","doc":"Hook-length product of `λ = (3,2)`: hooks `{4,3,2,1,1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hookProd41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hookProd41","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L72-L74","doc":"Hook-length product of `λ = (4,1)`: hooks `{5,3,2,1,1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hookProdRow5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hookProdRow5","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L68-L70","doc":"Hook-length product of `λ = (5)`: hooks `{5,4,3,2,1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_five","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L62-L66","doc":"`[5]_q! = [1][2][3][4][5]` — the q-factorial expanded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qIntGeo_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qIntGeo_one","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneQBesselRadialTarget.lean#L58-L60","doc":"`[1]_q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}